3295:libs/alglib/src/ap.cpp **** /************************************************************************
3296:libs/alglib/src/ap.cpp **** This function atomically appends pointer to arr, increasing array  length
3297:libs/alglib/src/ap.cpp **** by 1 and returns index of the element being added.
3298:libs/alglib/src/ap.cpp **** 
3299:libs/alglib/src/ap.cpp **** arr                 array.
3300:libs/alglib/src/ap.cpp **** ptr                 smart pointer structure
3301:libs/alglib/src/ap.cpp **** 
3302:libs/alglib/src/ap.cpp **** Notes:
3303:libs/alglib/src/ap.cpp **** * if array has fixed capacity and its size is already at  its  limit,  an
3304:libs/alglib/src/ap.cpp ****   exception will be generated
3305:libs/alglib/src/ap.cpp **** * ptr can be NULL
3306:libs/alglib/src/ap.cpp **** * non-NULL ptr MUST own its value prior to calling this function, and  it
3307:libs/alglib/src/ap.cpp ****   will transfer ownership to arr after the call (although it will   still
3308:libs/alglib/src/ap.cpp ****   point to the object)
3309:libs/alglib/src/ap.cpp **** * non-NULL ptr must point  to the dynamically  allocated object (on-stack
3310:libs/alglib/src/ap.cpp ****   objects are not supported)
3311:libs/alglib/src/ap.cpp **** 
3312:libs/alglib/src/ap.cpp **** This function is partially thread-safe:
3313:libs/alglib/src/ap.cpp **** * parallel threads can concurrently append elements using this function
3314:libs/alglib/src/ap.cpp **** * for fixed-capacity arrays it is possible to combine appends with reads,
3315:libs/alglib/src/ap.cpp ****   e.g. to use ae_obj_array_get()
3316:libs/alglib/src/ap.cpp **** ************************************************************************/
3317:libs/alglib/src/ap.cpp **** ae_int_t ae_obj_array_append_transfer(ae_obj_array *arr, ae_smart_ptr *ptr, ae_state *state)
3318:libs/alglib/src/ap.cpp **** {
