12753:libs/alglib/src/ap.cpp **** /*************************************************************************
12754:libs/alglib/src/ap.cpp **** This function calculates MxN real matrix-vector product:
12755:libs/alglib/src/ap.cpp **** 
12756:libs/alglib/src/ap.cpp ****     y := beta*y + alpha*A*x
12757:libs/alglib/src/ap.cpp **** 
12758:libs/alglib/src/ap.cpp **** using generic C code. It calls _ialglib_mv_32 if both M=32 and N=32.
12759:libs/alglib/src/ap.cpp **** 
12760:libs/alglib/src/ap.cpp **** If beta is zero, we do not use previous values of y (they are  overwritten
12761:libs/alglib/src/ap.cpp **** by alpha*A*x without ever being read).  If alpha is zero, no matrix-vector
12762:libs/alglib/src/ap.cpp **** product is calculated (only beta is updated); however, this update  is not
12763:libs/alglib/src/ap.cpp **** efficient  and  this  function  should  NOT  be used for multiplication of 
12764:libs/alglib/src/ap.cpp **** vector and scalar.
12765:libs/alglib/src/ap.cpp **** 
12766:libs/alglib/src/ap.cpp **** IMPORTANT:
12767:libs/alglib/src/ap.cpp **** * 0<=M<=alglib_r_block, 0<=N<=alglib_r_block
12768:libs/alglib/src/ap.cpp **** * A must be stored in row-major order with stride equal to alglib_r_block
12769:libs/alglib/src/ap.cpp **** * y may be non-aligned
12770:libs/alglib/src/ap.cpp **** * both A and x must have same offset with respect to 16-byte boundary:
12771:libs/alglib/src/ap.cpp ****   either both are aligned, or both are aligned with offset 8. Function
12772:libs/alglib/src/ap.cpp ****   will crash your system if you try to call it with misaligned or 
12773:libs/alglib/src/ap.cpp ****   incorrectly aligned data.
12774:libs/alglib/src/ap.cpp **** 
12775:libs/alglib/src/ap.cpp **** This function supports SSE2; it can be used when:
12776:libs/alglib/src/ap.cpp **** 1. AE_HAS_SSE2_INTRINSICS was defined (checked at compile-time)
12777:libs/alglib/src/ap.cpp **** 2. ae_cpuid() result contains CPU_SSE2 (checked at run-time)
12778:libs/alglib/src/ap.cpp **** 
12779:libs/alglib/src/ap.cpp **** If (1) is failed, this function will be undefined. If (2) is failed,  call 
12780:libs/alglib/src/ap.cpp **** to this function will probably crash your system. 
12781:libs/alglib/src/ap.cpp **** 
12782:libs/alglib/src/ap.cpp **** If  you  want  to  know  whether  it  is safe to call it, you should check 
12783:libs/alglib/src/ap.cpp **** results  of  ae_cpuid(). If CPU_SSE2 bit is set, this function is callable 
12784:libs/alglib/src/ap.cpp **** and will do its work.
12785:libs/alglib/src/ap.cpp **** *************************************************************************/
12786:libs/alglib/src/ap.cpp **** #if defined(AE_HAS_SSE2_INTRINSICS)
