18577:libs/alglib/src/ap.cpp **** /*************************************************************************
18578:libs/alglib/src/ap.cpp **** Fast kernels for small supernodal updates: special 4x4x4x4 function.
18579:libs/alglib/src/ap.cpp **** 
18580:libs/alglib/src/ap.cpp **** ! See comments on UpdateSupernode() for information  on generic supernodal
18581:libs/alglib/src/ap.cpp **** ! updates, including notation used below.
18582:libs/alglib/src/ap.cpp **** 
18583:libs/alglib/src/ap.cpp **** The generic update has following form:
18584:libs/alglib/src/ap.cpp **** 
18585:libs/alglib/src/ap.cpp ****     S := S - scatter(U*D*Uc')
18586:libs/alglib/src/ap.cpp **** 
18587:libs/alglib/src/ap.cpp **** This specialized function performs AxBxCx4 update, i.e.:
18588:libs/alglib/src/ap.cpp **** * S is a tHeight*A matrix with row stride equal to 4 (usually it means that
18589:libs/alglib/src/ap.cpp ****   it has 3 or 4 columns)
18590:libs/alglib/src/ap.cpp **** * U is a uHeight*B matrix
18591:libs/alglib/src/ap.cpp **** * Uc' is a B*C matrix, with C<=A
18592:libs/alglib/src/ap.cpp **** * scatter() scatters rows and columns of U*Uc'
18593:libs/alglib/src/ap.cpp ****   
18594:libs/alglib/src/ap.cpp **** Return value:
18595:libs/alglib/src/ap.cpp **** * True if update was applied
18596:libs/alglib/src/ap.cpp **** * False if kernel refused to perform an update (quick exit for unsupported
18597:libs/alglib/src/ap.cpp ****   combinations of input sizes)
18598:libs/alglib/src/ap.cpp **** 
