18890:libs/alglib/src/ap.cpp **** 
18891:libs/alglib/src/ap.cpp **** /*************************************************************************
18892:libs/alglib/src/ap.cpp **** Fast kernels for small supernodal updates: special 4x4x4x4 function.
18893:libs/alglib/src/ap.cpp **** 
18894:libs/alglib/src/ap.cpp **** ! See comments on UpdateSupernode() for information  on generic supernodal
18895:libs/alglib/src/ap.cpp **** ! updates, including notation used below.
18896:libs/alglib/src/ap.cpp **** 
18897:libs/alglib/src/ap.cpp **** The generic update has following form:
18898:libs/alglib/src/ap.cpp **** 
18899:libs/alglib/src/ap.cpp ****     S := S - scatter(U*D*Uc')
18900:libs/alglib/src/ap.cpp **** 
18901:libs/alglib/src/ap.cpp **** This specialized function performs 4x4x4x4 update, i.e.:
18902:libs/alglib/src/ap.cpp **** * S is a tHeight*4 matrix
18903:libs/alglib/src/ap.cpp **** * U is a uHeight*4 matrix
18904:libs/alglib/src/ap.cpp **** * Uc' is a 4*4 matrix
18905:libs/alglib/src/ap.cpp **** * scatter() scatters rows of U*Uc', but does not scatter columns (they are
18906:libs/alglib/src/ap.cpp ****   densely packed).
18907:libs/alglib/src/ap.cpp ****   
18908:libs/alglib/src/ap.cpp **** Return value:
18909:libs/alglib/src/ap.cpp **** * True if update was applied
18910:libs/alglib/src/ap.cpp **** * False if kernel refused to perform an update.
18911:libs/alglib/src/ap.cpp **** 
18912:libs/alglib/src/ap.cpp ****   -- ALGLIB routine --
